extends /specs/page-structure/layout.jade

block content
    h1 Sticko
    p Make any element sticky using HTML Classes

    section.source_section
        h2 Usage
        p Use HTMl Classes to control Sticko
        h3 Basic Sticky Element
        code.src-html.source_visible.source_example
            | <header class="sticko">
            |   ... header code over here ...
            | </header>
        p Adding "sticko" to any element will make it sticky all the time, its dimensions will be related to the "body" in other words the element's width will be fluid.
            | This approach has been used in UX3 sticky header Please visit Article template page.
        h3 Contained Sticky Element
        code.src-html.source_visible.source_example
            | <div class="col-md-4 col-xs-1 sticko__parent">
            |   <div class="tab sticko tab--slide">
            |       ... some content over here ...
            |   </div>
            | </div>
        p Adding "sticko__parent" to any parent element will make "sticko" element dimensions be related to that parent element.
            | This class has been used in article page side bar tabs.
        h3 Responsive Sticky Element
        code.src-html.source_visible.source_example
            | <div class="col-md-4 col-xs-1 sticko__parent">
            |   <div class="tab sticko__md tab--slide">
            |       ... some content over here ...
            |   </div>
            | </div>
        p Adding "sticko-md" to any element will make it sticky in medium and large screens.
        h3 Dynamic Sticky Element
        code.src-html.source_visible.source_example
            | <div class="col-md-4 col-xs-1 sticko__parent">
            |   <div class="tab sticko__md tab--slide">
            |       <ul class=" rlist--inline tab__nav">
            |           ... some content over here ...
            |       </ul>
            |       <div class="tab__content sticko__child">
            |           ... some content goes overhere ...
            |       </div>
            |   </div>
            | </div>
        p Adding "sticko__child" to one of it's direct children will make it scrollable and has a dynamic height, in other words the height of the "sticko__child" will be affected when ever "scroll" event has been triggered.
    | #{''}